--TEST--
A `throw` of an anonymous object, or of a parameter typed with a shape, does not compile, since no `catch` matches it — `rule:errors/throwable-hierarchy`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Shop {
    public static function fail(): void {
        // Refused: an anonymous object is not a `Throwable`.
        throw {class: "X", message: "m"};
    }

    public static function again({message: string} $error): void {
        // Refused: a shape is not a `Throwable`.
        throw $error;
    }

    public static function rethrow(?RuntimeError $error): void {
        // Accepted: a nullable class of the tree.
        if ($error != null) {
            throw $error;
        }
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0780]: `throw` takes a `Throwable`, and `%s` is not one
%A
error[E0780]: `throw` takes a `Throwable`, and `%s` is not one
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
